### Description

#### Problem
Some messages coming from the processing pipeline are too big for nats to handle (exceeds the nats messages max payload size)

#### Solution
When pulling those messages from proxy, the PullWorker will store them in the storage (GCS) and then it will send a much shorter message the consumer via nats (on a new stream) that points to the broker message.
The new consumer will read the message from nats, get the pointer and retrieve the broker message from the storage to process it.

#### Implementation details:
As we are initially adding this under a feature flag, I've opted adding a new separate stream (`ndb.consumer.processed-v2"`) and adding a new set of processed-consumer deployments that will consume from the new stream.

The pull worker will send to the `v2` stream only if the feature is enabled.

Once we are confident that it works well, I will replace the old stream and consumers with the `v2` ones.

```mermaid
graph TD;
    Proxy --> PullWorker;
    PullWorker -- FF is on --> STREAM-v2;
    PullWorker -- FF off --> STREAM;
    STREAM-v2 --> Consumer-v2;
    STREAM --> Consumer;
```

